            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "{\"duration_s\": 83.894, \"duration\": \"01:24\", \"summary\": \"This educational animation illustrates the scientific mechanism behind how mRNA COVID-19 vaccines protect the body. It shows how the vaccine prompts human cells to generate harmless viral spike proteins, triggering the immune system to produce antibodies that neutralize future viral threats.\", \"subjects\": [{\"name\": \"Coronavirus\", \"kind\": \"other\", \"description\": \"Graphic illustration of the COVID-19 virus with outer spike proteins.\", \"first_seen\": \"00:01\"}, {\"name\": \"mRNA Vaccine\", \"kind\": \"object\", \"description\": \"A syringe containing messenger RNA lipid nanoparticles designed to instruct cells.\", \"first_seen\": \"00:19\"}, {\"name\": \"Antibodies\", \"kind\": \"other\", \"description\": \"Y-shaped immune system proteins that bind to coronavirus spike proteins to neutralize the virus.\", \"first_seen\": \"00:43\"}], \"chapters\": [{\"start\": \"00:00\", \"end\": \"00:19\", \"title\": \"Viral Spikes as a Target\", \"summary\": \"Explains how the COVID-19 virus binds to host cells using spike proteins, creating a key target for vaccines.\"}, {\"start\": \"00:19\", \"end\": \"00:45\", \"title\": \"mRNA Vaccine Function\", \"summary\": \"Shows how the mRNA vaccine directs cells to produce harmless spike proteins, alerting the immune system.\"}, {\"start\": \"00:45\", \"end\": \"01:02\", \"title\": \"Neutralizing the Virus\", \"summary\": \"Demonstrates how generated antibodies surround and bind to the coronavirus spikes, neutralizing the infection.\"}, {\"start\": \"01:02\", \"end\": \"01:24\", \"title\": \"Safety and Conclusion\", \"summary\": \"Summarizes the rigorous study and safety of mRNA vaccines, followed by production credits.\"}]}"
              }
