            "text": "The video explains how mRNA vaccines work, so the answer is A.\n\n- **[00:00–00:19]** It shows how the COVID-19 virus uses its spike proteins to attach to human cells. That makes the spikes the target for a vaccine.\n- **[00:19–00:45]** The mRNA vaccine tells cells to make harmless spike proteins, which alerts the immune system.\n- **[00:45–01:02]** The antibodies the body makes then bind to the virus's spikes and neutralize it.\n- **[01:02–01:24]** It closes with a short note that the vaccines have been carefully studied and are safe, then the credits.\n\nThe video doesn't cover how the vaccines are produced, their market, or their side effects. This comes from the video's chapter summaries; I didn't check individual frames.\n\nAnswer: A"
